Function: dict_filter

Specification: Write a function dict_filter(dict1, n) that filters a dictionary to only the entries with values greater than or equal to n. Return the entries ordered by value from highest to lowest (dictionary insertion order).

Acceptance tests:
test_1: assert dict_filter({'Cierra Vega': 175, 'Alden Cantrell': 180, 'Kierra Gentry': 165, 'Pierre Cox': 190},180)=={ 'Alden Cantrell': 180, 'Pierre Cox': 190}
test_2: assert dict_filter({'Cierra Vega': 175, 'Alden Cantrell': 180, 'Kierra Gentry': 165, 'Pierre Cox': 190},190)=={ 'Pierre Cox': 190}
test_3: assert list(dict_filter({'a': 1, 'c': 3, 'b': 5}, 2).items()) == [('b', 5), ('c', 3)]
test_4: assert dict_filter({'Cierra Vega': 175, 'Alden Cantrell': 180, 'Kierra Gentry': 165, 'Pierre Cox': 190},170)=={'Cierra Vega': 175, 'Alden Cantrell': 180, 'Pierre Cox': 190}
